-- title:
--   Full-kernel Vélu quotient: pushforward point map has kernel ℤQ
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ whose affine model is elliptic, let $Q$ be a point of that affine curve and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number with $\operatorname{addOrderOf} Q = N$. Write $W'$ for `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N`, the Vélu quotient of $W$ formed from the two sums, over $P$ in `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (N - 1)`, of $g_x(P)$ and of $x_P g_x(P) - y_P g_y(P)$. Assume the discriminant of $W'$ is nonzero and that $W'$ is elliptic, and assume for each of $W$ and $W'$ the interface data: a `GenusOnePlaceGate`, i.e. a bijection between the affine points and the places of the function field over $F$ together with the assertion that every such place has degree $1$; its centredness, i.e. for every nonsingular $(x,y)$ the classes of $X-x$ and $Y-y$ lie in the nonunits of the valuation subring of the place attached to that point; and `AbelTheorem`, i.e. a degree-zero divisor is principal exactly when its divisor sum vanishes. Then there exist an $F$-algebra homomorphism $\iota : F(W') \to F(W)$, a proof that $\iota$ is integral, and a proof that $F(W)$ is a finite module over $F(W')$ via $\iota$, such that for every witness of the pushforward norm formula along $\iota$ (for every nonzero $f \in F(W)$ with divisor $D$ and every place $v$ of $F(W')$, the pushforward of $D$ at $v$ equals $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the norm of $f$), the homomorphism `pointMapOfPushforward` $W(F) \to W'(F)$ — transport of a point to its class in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, pushforward of degree-zero divisor classes along $\iota$, and transport back — has kernel exactly `AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q`, the subgroup of integer multiples of $Q$.
--
--   This is the level-$N$ form, with no parity hypothesis on $N$, of the statement that the Vélu quotient by the cyclic subgroup generated by a point $Q$ of order $N$ carries an isogeny from $W$ whose kernel is precisely $\langle Q\rangle$, realised here through pushforward of divisor classes along the corresponding function-field embedding. It is used in the construction of cyclic $N$-isogenies from Tate points on modular curves, by [`ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelInjAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelInjAt) and [`ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_functionFieldHom_fullKernelQuotient_pointMapOfPushforward_ker_eq_zmultiples.lean

import Mathlib
